# shelf: kneemri-members-2
# out: members_2
#
# comp/members2.roster — the SECOND weights dataset, `kneemri-members-2`, mounted BESIDE the shipped one.
#
# WHY A SECOND PACKAGE EXISTS. The shipped package holds 127 members and about 10 GB. Adding one member
# to it means re-pushing all ten gigabytes, which nobody does per member — so every member trained after
# the last big push was an offline gain that could never become a board gain. This file holds only the
# members added since that push. `MemberPackage.spanning` merges every mounted root into one package and
# REFUSES an identifier two roots both hold, so a member listed here must NOT also be in
# `comp/members.roster`: a duplicate is not a merge conflict, it is a vote loading weights nobody chose.
#
# A member here is still governed by `roster_check` and by `comp/members.declines` — this is a second
# SHELF, never a second standard.

# The highest solo this project owns: band_dense's recipe distilled from our own out-of-fold posterior
# at weight 0.7. Reads 0.8681 against band_dense's 0.8578, and the gain sits on the model-bottlenecked
# findings (MCL +0.0310, Lateral Meniscus +0.0250, ACL +0.0175, Contusion +0.0175). Its one
# pre-registered prediction — synovitis — FAILED at -0.0040, which is what says this is an ordering
# transfer rather than a calibration effect.
oof_teacher_s2026.pt                 # 0.8681

# The v4b label TABLE, carried by a member so the board can read it. Its offline number is not a
# quality reading and must not be quoted as one: it is scored on report_labels_v2, so every place the
# v4b grading DISAGREES with v2 is charged to it as an error (0.8524 against band_dense's 0.8578,
# -0.0054 that is a disagreement rate and not a loss). On gold-58 the table it trains on leads v2 by
# +0.0337, and that census shares an origin with the table, so neither ruler can settle it. The board
# is the third ruler and the only independent one — this member exists to be read there, as a solo,
# against holdsolo (0.8634 offline, 0.928 board).
labels_v4hybrid_s2026.pt             # 0.8524 on the v2 ruler — a disagreement rate, see above

# The leak-free re-read of the distillation term: band_dense's recipe distilled from teachers built
# with --exclude-fold 0, so no teacher ever saw the fold it is scored on. 0.8634 against band_dense's
# 0.8578 and against its own leaky twin seat_distill_lr4e5's 0.8633 — it matched the twin out of
# teachers that are -0.0067 weaker by construction, which is what says the +0.0107 is a treatment
# effect and not memorised fold-0 labels (knee-zwcyk). Seated as the honest member of that family.
seat_clean_distill_s2026.pt          # 0.8634

# The leak removed by dropping the HOLDOUT rather than by weakening the teachers: fitted at --fold -1
# against teacher_oof5.npz, five REAL out-of-fold blocks covering all 4406 studies, each predicting only
# the fold it held out. No evaluation set is left for a memorised label to leak into, by construction —
# and by the same construction this member has NO offline number and can never have one. Its ruler is
# the board (kneemri-oof5solo, pre-registered against holdsolo's 0.928). Its held-out twin
# seat_clean_distill read 0.8634, matching the leaky 0.8633 out of teachers -0.0067 weaker, which is
# what says the term being shipped here is a treatment effect. knee-zwcyk
seat_oof5_distill_s2026.pt           # no offline number by construction, --fold -1

# The two calibrated-distill twins that were trained, converged, and sat on NO roster line for four
# days. They are on THIS shelf and not the shipped one for the reason this file exists: adding a member
# to `kneemri-members` is a 14 GB re-push (measured at all_ours today) onto a disk with 38 GB free,
# which is exactly the cost that made every member trained after the last big push unshippable. They
# were first written onto the first shelf and moved here the same hour; a kernel seating either one must
# declare BOTH mounts, and `mount_check` refuses it on the shelf line if it declares only the first.
#
# NEITHER HAS AN OFFLINE NUMBER AND NEITHER EVER WILL — both fitted at `--fold -1`, so they hold nothing
# out and no offline ruler can read them, the same construction as `seat_oof5_distill_s2026` above.
# `final_ws_df` is the whole-corpus calibrated-distill seat: 336 px / 20 slices / band 0.1-0.9, --ema,
# --calibrated-targets, --distill-weight 0.7 on teacher_oof5.npz, 12 epochs, converged (13 rows in its
# metrics.jsonl = recipe plus twelve). ITS STAND-IN IS `clean_calib_s2026` — fold 0, same corner — and
# the stand-in is TWO knobs away, not one: the teacher FILE (clean vs oof5) and `--ema`, which
# final_ws_df carries and clean_calib.sh does not (researcher D34). `ema` is UNPRICED at this corner and
# no one-knob pair exists on disk, so clean_calib's paired delta against seat_clean_distill_s2026 on the
# 909 under LEDGER75 is the best price this seat can be given — an approximate one, and it is what
# licences seating it. `arm_check` refused a second name for this exact recipe (clean_calib_cf,
# knee-7uoq) and saved 75 minutes of card by doing it.
final_ws_df.pt                       # no offline number by construction, --fold -1

# The narrow-span twin of the seat above — 12 slices at band 0.1-0.9 against final_ws_df's 20 at the
# same band — so the pair prices SPAN at the calibrated-distill corner and nothing else. Its stand-in
# has not been named: the researcher owes which fold-0 member differs from it in the teacher file alone.
# Until then it may be packaged but not seated on a number.
calib_span_df.pt                     # no offline number by construction, --fold -1

# Added 2026-09-07 17:55Z, out of comp/members.declines (see the re-opening written there). 0.8577 solo,
# CONVERGED (twelve of twelve, peak epoch 4, then eight declining epochs) -- a WORSE solo than every
# seated member, and seated anyway. The argument is decorrelation, not quality: D45 reads it at +0.0009
# as an extra seat in the ours-side block at corr 0.898, and D45's three-seat stack (this member,
# labelwise_dense_s2026 and warm_calib_dense_s2026, all three added to the block, raptor's 1/3 untouched)
# at +0.0026 offline. It ships because of D50: on the 36 rebuildable board rows a common-frame rebuilt
# L75mid predicts the board at R2 0.962 with resid SD 0.0016, which is what makes +0.0026 readable at all.
# The other two seats are already on shelf 1; this one is on NEITHER shelf, which is the whole reason for
# this line. It is an INSTRUMENT seat, priced on a fit whose band (0.904-0.937) does not include the
# champion's 0.944 -- the extrapolation is stated in the kernel's pre-registration, not hidden here.
warm_calib_lowlr_s2026.pt            # 0.8577 solo; seated on decorrelation, +0.0009 as an extra seat

# Added 2026-09-07 18:05Z for the D45 three-seat stack (kneemri-stack). The FULL-FIT twin of
# labelwise_dense_s2026 -- fold -1, --ema, otherwise the identical recipe (labelwise pooling,
# calibrated targets, v2 labels, lr 4e-5, lora 0, whole_stack). It has sat on disk since 2026-08-31
# 05:17Z, converged (13 rows in metrics.jsonl, epoch 11 of 12), on NO roster and in NO ledger section,
# unshippable for the reason this shelf exists. Its own arm declares it `# unmeasurable:` -- fitted at
# --fold -1, so it holds nothing out and no offline ruler can read it, ever. It is seated on its fold-0
# twin's number and on the D35 sixth-seat fit, which prices a full-fit seat about +0.0002 of block delta
# above the fold-0 one (~+0.0029 solo lift, 0.076 pass-through). That is fit arithmetic, not a
# measurement, and it moves the stack's +0.0026 by less than its own bootstrap width.
labelwise_dense_ff.pt                # no offline number by construction, --fold -1; twin reads 0.8959

